  "reason": "With no completed experiments, the most critical uncertainty is establishing a performance floor: how well can we do with the simplest viable model? config_026 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000, no image, no aggregation, no fusion) is the minimal baseline that isolates raw RNA signal quality. It uses PCA (fast, standard) and a single profile to avoid confounding from learned encoders, multiprofile aggregation, or fusion. This single experiment gives a clean reference against which every subsequent design choice—image modality, learned RNA encoders (scvi/scgpt), multiprofile aggregation, and fusion strategy—can be measured. Starting here respects the principle of not assuming complexity helps, keeps the first experiment fast and interpretable, and maximizes the information gained per experiment by anchoring all future comparisons to a well-defined floor."
}

